        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set offers a curated list of six strategic research topics centered on **Black Holes**, ranging from stellar-mass to supermassive scale, with a strong emphasis on their functional roles in the universe. Each topic is formulated to support a comprehensive academic report by focusing on complex relationships, critical mechanisms, and deep theoretical implications. The subjects move beyond mere definition, exploring areas such as the quantum-gravity conflict at the event horizon, the efficiency of energy conversion in accretion disks, and the role of gravitational wave astronomy as a new observational paradigm. The framework ensures that each topic can be developed across the five essential analytical sections: Historical Context, Foundational Principles, Mechanisms & Processes, Evidence & Manifestations, and Broader Implications.",
