        },
        {
          "text": "**Primordial Black Holes (PBHs):** The theoretical possibility of black holes forming in the radiation-dominated era of the early universe, and their potential to constitute a fraction of Dark Matter.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 94,
          "source": "topic-set-black-hole-astrophysics-and-the-extreme-gravity-universe-🆔20251026011736.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The No-Hair Theorem:** The foundational concept that a stationary black hole can be completely characterized by only three externally observable parameters: mass, electric charge, and angular momentum (spin).",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 94,
          "source": "topic-set-black-hole-astrophysics-and-the-extreme-gravity-universe-🆔20251026011736.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Tidal Disruption Events (TDEs):** The violent mechanism that occurs when a star passes too close to a supermassive black hole and is ripped apart by tidal forces, providing a brief flare of light as evidence of an otherwise quiescent black hole.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 97,
          "source": "topic-set-black-hole-astrophysics-and-the-extreme-gravity-universe-🆔20251026011736.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**X-ray Binaries and Microquasars:** Stellar-mass black holes in binary systems that exhibit scaled-down versions of the jet and accretion phenomena seen in supermassive black holes.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 108,
          "source": "topic-set-black-hole-astrophysics-and-the-extreme-gravity-universe-🆔20251026011736.md"
        }
      ]
